<title>USA: American may modify Boeing order.</title>
<headline>American may modify Boeing order.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Robert Crandall, chairman of American Airlines, a unit of AMR Corp, said Monday the carrier would have to modify its order for new aircraft made by Boeing Co if a satisfactory labor agreement was not reached with airline pilots.</p>
<p>The airline had said when it placed the $6.6 billion  order last November that making it final would be contingent on a new labor pact with the carrier's pilots.</p>
<p>American Airlines is in negotiations with the union on a new agreement.</p>
<p>Asked at an aviation conference whether he had discussed the planned purchase with Boeing, Crandall said he had had very good discussions with the carrier.</p>
<p>But he added &quot;obviously, if we can't find a satisfactory agreeement with the pilots, we'll have to modify the order.&quot;</p>
</text>
